  {
    "claim": "Anthropic's Messages API cannot be reached through the OPENAI arm: it is a distinct wire, not chat-completions with a different key.",
    "detail": "Five differences, any one of which 400s: the key rides x-api-key (not Authorization: Bearer) and anthropic-version is required; the system prompt is a top-level `system` param, not a role:\"system\" message; max_tokens is REQUIRED and has no server-side default; tools carry `input_schema` rather than `parameters`; and tool traffic is tool_use / tool_result CONTENT BLOCKS inside user/assistant turns, never a role:\"tool\" message. <ARM>_HEADERS can fix the header and nothing else. Hence the ANTHROPIC arm and the `anthropic` dialect - the same lesson the GEMINI arm already taught.",
    "tags": "llm,anthropic,dialect,resolver",
    "source": {
      "doc": "agent.llm.chat_llm"
    },
    "confidence": "high",
    "time": 1786878897877
  },
  {
    "claim": "With thinking on, an Anthropic assistant turn that called a tool is rejected on the NEXT request unless its thinking block is replayed verbatim and first.",
    "detail": "Thinking is ON BY DEFAULT on Opus 5 (omitting the `thinking` param runs adaptive), so this fires on the very first tool call rather than only under an opt-in. parse_anthropic keeps the raw thinking/redacted_thinking blocks on the assistant_message as `thinking_blocks`, and build_anthropic_payload re-emits them as the first entries of the assistant content array - the same carry-it-on-the-replay-object trick Gemini's thought_signature uses. Dropping them, or ordering them after text/tool_use, breaks the turn. display:\"omitted\" (the default) still returns the block with an empty `thinking` string and a live signature: it is the signature that matters, not the text.",
    "tags": "llm,anthropic,thinking,tool-loop",
    "source": {
      "doc": "agent.llm.chat_llm"
    },
    "confidence": "high",
    "time": 1786878898049
